//! task: fix
//! ask: Write a function returning the smaller of two u64 values.
//! expect: EXS-E0201,EXS-E0303
//! primary: EXS-E0201
//! refs: §8.4, §8.6 decision 6
//! explain: `<` and `>` are never operators in Exsecutor: they delimit generic arguments, and comparison is the contextual words `lt le gt ge eq ne`. The `EXS-E0303` after the first diagnostic is recovery cascade from the unparsed condition, and disappears with the fix.

publica functio minimum(a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 {
    si a < b {
        redde a;
    }
    redde b;
}
//@ fixed
publica functio minimum(a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 {
    si a lt b {
        redde a;
    }
    redde b;
}
